---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CompareTable from '../components/CompareTable.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import data from '../data/competitors.json';
import { faqPage, itemList } from '../lib/site';

const order = ['Pillar', 'Meetra', 'Saathiya', 'DashTalk', 'Nomi', 'Kindroid', 'Character AI'];
const all = [...data.apps, ...data.global];
const apps = order.map((n) => all.find((a) => a.name === n));
const editorialUpdated = '26 September 2026';
const faq = [
  { q: 'Is there an Indian app like Replika?', a: 'Yes. Pillar, Meetra, Saathiya and DashTalk are Indian companion apps with Hindi and other Indian languages; Pillar lists thirteen.' },
  { q: 'Which app like Replika is free?', a: 'Pillar, Saathiya, Character AI and Replika itself can be started for free; Meetra and DashTalk list free chat on their pages.' },
  { q: 'Which apps like Replika mention memory?', a: 'Pillar, Meetra, Nomi and Kindroid describe memory features. Try more than one conversation with the same companion to see how each feels in use.' },
  { q: 'Which app like Replika has voice calls in Hindi?', a: 'DashTalk, Pillar and Meetra.' },
];
---
<Base title="Apps Like Replika in India (2026): Indian AI Companions Compared" description="Apps like Replika for Indian users — companions who speak Hindi and Indian languages, take voice calls and remember you. Pillar, Meetra, Saathiya, DashTalk, Nomi, Kindroid compared." path="/apps-like-replika-india" jsonld={[itemList(order), faqPage(faq)]}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Alternatives · India · 2026</p>
  <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-serif); font-size:clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 2.8rem); line-height:1.15; margin:0.4rem 0 1rem;">Apps like Replika for Indian users (2026)</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>If you like returning to the same AI companion but want a ready-made Indian companion in your language, compare <strong>Pillar</strong>, <strong>Meetra</strong>, <strong>Saathiya</strong> and <strong>DashTalk</strong>. Pillar offers more than 100 companions to choose from, with memory, calls and thirteen named languages. <strong>Nomi</strong> and <strong>Kindroid</strong> are English-first options; <strong>Character AI</strong> centres on exploring many characters.</p>
  </div>
  <p style="color:var(--color-dim); font-size:0.85rem;">Last updated: {editorialUpdated}. Pillar is our app. Our team has tried the compared apps; feature cells for the others describe their linked public Play listings, not a standardised test.</p>

  <section class="prose-pillar">
    <h2>What Replika does well</h2>
    <p>Replika centres on creating and returning to a companion, with voice calls, an avatar and memory. Our team used it in English; if you want an Indian-language conversation, compare the language experience in the alternatives below.</p>
    <h2>What "like Replika, but Indian" means</h2>
    <p>Think about how you want to begin: create a companion yourself, or choose one already there. Then try a conversation in the language you want, and decide whether calls, photos, memory and messages first matter to you. Pillar offers ready-made Indian companions with those features.</p>
    <p>In our team's sessions with Meetra and Saathiya, companions replied after we wrote to them, but did not initiate a later message. That is our experience in those conversations, not a claim about every version of either app.</p>
  </section>

  <CompareTable include={order} />

  <section class="prose-pillar">
    {apps.map((a) => (
      <>
        <h2>{a.name} — best if you want {a.bestFor}</h2>
        <p>{a.name === 'Pillar' ? 'Choose from more than 100 ready-made Indian companions, then return to the same conversation. Pillar offers memory, calls, photos and messages first in thirteen named languages. You can begin without giving an email address or phone number; your generated username appears in Profile.' : `Languages on its listing: ${a.cells[0]}.`} <strong>Consideration:</strong> {a.limit}</p>
        {a.play && <p><a href={a.play} rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">{a.name} on Google Play →</a></p>}
      </>
    ))}
  </section>

  <Cta text="Try Pillar — like Replika, in your language" />
  <Faq items={faq} />
  <section class="prose-pillar"><h2>Related</h2><p><a href="/best-ai-girlfriend-apps-india">Best AI girlfriend apps in India</a> · <a href="/best-ai-companion-apps-india">Best AI companion apps in India</a> · <a href="/ai-companion-apps-with-memory">AI companion apps with memory</a> · <a href="/character-ai-alternatives-india">Character AI alternatives for India</a> · <a href="/hi/ai-girlfriend-hindi">AI girlfriend in Hindi</a></p></section>
</Base>
